Accessibility Audit: Ohio University Online

| **Website Tested** | Ohio University Online (homepage) |
|-------------------|-----------------------------------|
| **Test Date**     | June 3, 2026                      |
| **Tester**        | Ava Lundgren                      |
| **Tools Used**    | Axe DevTools, Lighthouse, WAVE    |
| **WCAG Baseline** | 2.1 Level A + AA                  |

---

## Executive Summary

**Most critical findings:** 4 very low contrast failures, 3 orphaned form labels and 1 broken ARIA tablist component. The tablist issue is the highest priority because it makes interactive content entirely unusable for screen reader and keyboard users.

**Overall accessibility posture:** High-risk for assistive technology users, specifically screen readers and low-visions users.

