## Conclusion

Ohio University Online has multiple high-severity accessibility failures that create real barriers for screen reader users, keyboard-only users and users with low vision. The broken ARIA tablist is the most critical issue as it demonstrates that ARIA was added without the complete required pattern, which can make components less accessible than native HTML.

